      "imagePrompt": "A microwave oven with invisible waves traveling through its interior toward a bowl of food."
    },
    {
      "title": "Water Molecules Wiggle",
      "text": "The waves’ changing electric field makes water molecules in the food turn and wiggle. Many foods contain water, so this motion can happen throughout a meal.",
      "imagePrompt": "A close-up of water molecules in food turning as changing electric waves pass through them."
    },
    {
      "title": "Motion Becomes Heat",
      "text": "As the molecules jostle nearby molecules, their motion spreads through the food as heat. It’s a bit like a crowd passing along a ripple, warming more than just one spot.",
